s":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"id\": \"creation_redemption_004_what_costs_do_the_creation_fee_cover\", \"points\": [{\"point\": 1, \"mark\": \"required\", \"minimum\": \"Must state that fixed creation/redemption charges cover processing, transfer and related operational/administrative costs of the transaction, AND that variable charges offset portfolio trading costs (at least one of brokerage, taxes, market impact or similar trading costs) arising when cash, partial-cash or non-standard/custom orders require the fund to trade, so that remaining shareholders are protected from dilution. Optional subdetails: an exhaustive list of cost types (brokerage, transfer taxes, stamp duty, market impact, spreads) and specific dollar or basis-point amounts.\"}, {\"point\": 2, \"mark\": \"required\", \"minimum\": \"Must state that the AP (the creating/redeeming party) bears the transaction charge unless it is waived or paid by another party, AND that recipients can differ: fixed charges may go to the custodian or another service provider while variable charges go to the fund (as in the cited Corgi SAI), with recipient and waiver terms being fund-specific per the prospectus/SAI. Optional subdetails: naming Corgi specifically; reduced charges for in-kind orders; caps on maximum charges.\"}, {\"point\": 3, \"mark\": \"required\", \"minimum\": \"Must state that these transaction charges are not compensation to the AP. They are paid by the AP, not to it, and they cover fund or service-provider costs. This must be kept distinct from whatever the AP earns, such as arbitrage profit or client commissions.\"}, {\"point\": 4, \"mark\": \"optional\", \"minimum\": \"Notes that sponsors/advisers often waive custom-redemption charges (practitioner observation from Rafa). The answer should not overstate this into a universal rule or claim that a waiver necessarily means the sponsor makes a cash payment. Accept fund-specific framing of waiver or adviser-payment terms. Optional subdetail: a waiver may simply mean the cost is not charged or is absorbed under fund-specific arrangements.\"}], \"central_errors\": [\"States or implies that the creation/redemption fee reimburses, compensates, or is paid to the AP. This includes reproducing the unreviewed Participants 'Costs' line.\", \"States that the fund or its remaining shareholders, rather than the AP, ordinarily bear the creation/redemption transaction charge.\", \"States that fixed and variable charges always go to the same recipient, or that the recipient is uniform across all US ETFs.\", \"Reverses the cost roles in a central way, for example claiming variable charges cover only fixed processing/custody costs and do not offset trading/market-impact costs, or that fixed charges are for market impact.\", \"Asserts that a sponsor waiver necessarily means the sponsor makes a cash payment of the fee, presented as a universal rule.\"], \"scoring_rule\": {\"correct\": \"All three required points (1-3) are met at their minimums and there is no central error. Point 4 is not needed for full credit, but if it is mentioned it must not be overstated.\", \"partial\": \"There is no central error, and at least one required point is fully met while one or more others are missing or only half-met. Bundled points 1 and 2 earn half-credit when only one half is covered (e.g., fixed costs but not variable, or AP bears the charge but recipients are not addressed). As a guide, partial applies when roughly 1.5 to 2.5 of the 3 required point-equivalents are covered.\", \"wrong\": \"Any central error is present, OR fewer than roughly 1.5 required point-equivalents are covered, e.g., the answer only says that fees exist without explaining what costs they cover or who bears them.\"}}","ttft_ms":13441,"type":"result","duration_ms":13460,"uuid":"d9a65ae2-9ad7-414c-9d13-1be3387e4bd1","ttft_stream_ms":1661,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":1661,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
